===Etymology===
{{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|redic|lang=ang}}, {{term|rædic}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|rādīce|lang=la}}, the ablative singular of {{term|rādix||root|lang=la}}; later readopted from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|radis|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|pt|en}} {{term|raditz|lang=pt}}, from Latin. Also see: ''[[eradicate]]''.
[[Image:Raphanus_sativus.jpg|thumb|right|200px|A bundle of European radishes.]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈɹadɪʃ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈɹædɪʃ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-radish.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es}}

# {{context|botany|lang=en}} The [[common radish]] (''[[species:Raphanus sativus|Raphanus sativus]]''), a [[fast]]-[[growing]] [[plant]] with a [[short]] [[edible]] [[taproot]]; {{context|cuisine|lang=en}} the [[taproot]] itself as a [[foodstuff]].
# {{context|botany|lang=en}} Any [[plant]] of the ''[[Raphanus]]'' [[genus]], [[including]] the [[East Asia]]n [[daikon]] and [[rat-tail radish]]es; {{context|cuisine|lang=en}} their [[taproot]]s.

